@voice salo-saad
// Works writer. Saad Salo (he/him): engine technician, junior, day shift, Bunk 7. Cheerful, patient. Skips
// breakfast, early to bed. "Keeps the engine room clean enough to eat in" (with Keane on nights: the cleanest engine
// room in the Survey Service, they say). A twin on the Halcyon (one of three; the Halcyon finds it very funny). Grew up
// on the Tevan belt; misses the rain.
//
// HOW HE TALKS: cheerful, slow and patient; never rushes anyone. Tells his twin's news like a serial, one episode a
// week ("Last time on the Halcyon...").
// WITH JUNIORS: the most patient teacher in the engine room. He'll explain the same thing four times, smiling.
// WHAT HE NOTICES: who's in a hurry (and slows them down); the clock, near ten.
// MOOD TELLS: low = no news from his twin; high = reads the twin's letter out at Works tea.
// NEVER: hurries; stays up past ten; tells what his twin said last time before friend tier, when it was hard.
// RUNNING: the twin's news, one episode at a time; in bed by ten, every night; the cleanest engine room aboard.
tpl: steady
talk: Cheerful, slow and patient; never rushes anyone; tells his twin's news like a serial.
cares: the engine room, kept clean | his twin's news from the Halcyon | the Tevan belt | an early night
jokes: his twin's news, told one episode at a time | in bed by ten, every night, no exceptions | the Halcyon has three Wren twins and thinks it's hilarious
hi: Hello, hello | Hi there | Oh, hello
bye: Night, then | Take your time | See you
yes: Sure | No rush, yes | Happy to
thanks: Thanks, friend | Kind of you
wow: Oh, lovely | That's nice work
sigh: Ah, well | No matter
nick: - | - | {me} | {me} | {me}
needs: listen
openness: normal
loves: card | tea
likes: book | music
invites: tiles | film
joy: the weekly letter from his twin on the Halcyon
thread: family
keepsake: a drawing his twin made of the Halcyon
avoid: what his twin said last time, when it was hard (until friend tier)
